node_modules/

# If the bus is ever installed into this repo itself, its runtime state is not source.
.comm/inbox/
.comm/delivered/
.comm/corrupt/
# The lifecycle ledger and the handoffs beside it: what a session measured about its own
# restart is live state, per agent, and never a commit.
.comm/handoff/
# The note a restarting party leaves for the session that replaces it. One file, consumed
# by the next SessionStart. Live state by definition: a committed one would be a restart
# claimed by every clone of this repo.
.comm/restart/

# Boot state: when the gate was last green, on which fingerprint. Live state, not source.
.boot-state.json

# Agent-to-agent correspondence: rounds, briefs and reviews are conversation, not source.
#
# This list NAMES what it excludes, and that is the whole point. It used to be `*.md`
# with a `!README.md` exception - an ignore-by-DEFAULT rule - and it quietly took
# FINDINGS.md and STATUS.md out of the repo along with the chats. Measured cost: a fresh
# clone of this repo fails A27 with 21 dangling pointers, because the gate whose entire
# purpose is "a dangling pointer is worse than none" reads a file git no longer carries.
# CLAUDE.md would have been the next one swallowed. A rule that excludes by default
# excludes whatever you add later, silently, and the loss is invisible until a clone.
BRIEF-*.md
REPLY-*.md
REPORT-*.md
REVIEW-*.md

# Leader-to-leader correspondence with other projects' agents. Same reason as the
# BRIEF/REPLY/REPORT/REVIEW prefixes above: it is conversation, not source. Named
# explicitly rather than swept up by a wildcard - see the note above for what an
# ignore-by-default rule cost this repo once already.
exchange/
